                <head>PE–22. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>By an exchange of notes at Washington on June 15, 1959, Peru and the United
                    States concluded an agreement for a five-year renewable loan of a dry dock to
                    Peru. The agreement provided that Peru assume the costs of the transfer of the
                    dry dock and make available the dry dock and its naval yard to naval vessels of
                    the United States and of Latin American nations that had concluded military
                    assistance agreements with the United States. For the text of the agreement, see
                    10 UST 1053. Documentation on its negotiation is in Department of State files
                    723.5-MSP and 723.5621.</p>
            </div>
